---
code: oracle-matched-zero-sites
when-fires: a LOADED oracle's `__is_converged` verdict never actually vouched a single site this run -- either its command word never appears anywhere in the book, or every invocation's argv declined. cli/main.rs oracle_matched_zero_sites_diagnostics, aggregated from the run's own final `Vouches` (never a second lift).
why: 30Qe:fruit-oracle-matched-zero-sites. The silent-decline value-evaporation detector (`KNOBS:kWARN` rich, tune-high): loading an oracle that never earns a chance to help is easy to do quietly (a typo'd pre-source path, a stale command word, a book that moved on) and easy to never notice, since nothing breaks. `{oracle}` carries the loaded oracle's own path. World-as-payload (`aid/CLAUDE.md` fixture tier): the trigger reads the run's WHOLE final vouch set, which this single-file consumer has no seat to reconstruct; the real firing route is proven separately by the whole-product round-trip case `crates/cli/tests/oracle-matched-zero-sites-round-trip.loom`.
---
